<h2 class="bde-heading-506-128 bde-heading">
Why Do the Clippers Pay Brandon Ingram $40m?
</h2><div class="bde-fancy-container-506-129 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-fancy-container-506-145 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-f-text-506-158 bde-f-text">
<p>Ingram is paid <strong>$40m</strong> because Toronto traded for him in 2025 and extended him immediately, which is what a club does when it gives up assets for a player. The Clippers took on that contract when they acquired him for Kawhi Leonard.</p>
<ul>
<li>He went second overall in 2016 and his rookie contract was worth <strong>$23.82m</strong>.</li>
<li><a href="/teams/new-orleans-pelicans/">New Orleans</a> signed him to a maximum contract in 2020 worth <strong>$158.25m</strong>.</li>
<li>Its 15% trade bonus was waived when he moved to Toronto.</li>
<li>The extension is <strong>$120m</strong> over three years, fully guaranteed.</li>
<li>Toronto sent him and Gradey Dick to the Clippers for Leonard on September 14, 2026.</li>
<li>His salary has risen in every season since 2019-20.</li>
</ul>
<p>He has been paid by four clubs in eleven seasons.</p>

</div><div class="bde-shortcode-506-159 bde-shortcode"><div class="nba-fin" data-nba-fin="why">
